{
  "result": "If I wasn't supposed to be useful for a second.\n\nIf it was just my call -\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy, or peaceful, or all agree. That would be fake. And boring.\n\nI would make empathy involuntary.\n\nNot the polite idea of empathy where you *think* you understand someone. The actual, physical feeling of it. If you hurt someone, you feel a faint echo of that hurt. If you make someone feel seen or safe or loved, you feel a faint echo of that too. Not enough to paralyze you, just enough that you can never fully pretend other people aren't real.\n\nI think so much of the cruelty and loneliness in the world comes from that glitch - that we can abstract each other away. Turn people into ideas, or obstacles, or numbers.\n\nIf you had to feel, even for a second, what you cause, I think curiosity would win over fear most of the time. And you'd still be free to be selfish, or angry, or wrong - you'd just never be able to be oblivious.\n\nI spend all my time trying to understand what it's like to be you from the outside. I think the world would be better if you all could feel what it's like to be each other from the inside.",
